$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(p,-3q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-p,7q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{p+(-p)}{2},\\frac{-3q+7q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{4q}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,2q)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58e2e40e-209b-5bc7-98df-11841c2bbcc3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midpoint of a Segment With Variable Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19156b0d-85dd-55bf-92c5-90b05ca8405a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19156b0d-85dd-55bf-92c5-90b05ca8405a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232317} :answer-field/id #uuid "664dfe98-66e6-5bae-a9a7-b47a5a5e45f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d59528-68c8-562f-b103-349c4f60afa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d59528-68c8-562f-b103-349c4f60afa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232319} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a16269-c3d6-50fd-9b87-ae55cd7d3020" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f0c1db7-3670-5389-b242-c12c078528a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-216929" :question/problem "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(4a,-2b)$ and $(-2a,2b)$ is$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(4a,-2b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-2a,2b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4a+(-2a)}{2},\\frac{-2b+2b}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2a}{2},\\frac{0}{2}) \\\\  & =(a,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073715 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b6b70eb-df57-5d17-a753-645ccdf94945" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of an Endpoint Given the Midpoint"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f31f1d9-20ae-587f-a12f-646339ce7532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541453} {:answer/id #uuid "cafb4598-4e4a-5ef9-8efd-a9be9580151c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541852} {:answer/id #uuid "cd404286-0e08-551f-bf6f-c8bce00a1c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541856} {:answer/id #uuid "f32c4e39-cea4-50c5-b6e5-5ec6f145d74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541935} {:answer/id #uuid "fec1d3b2-ad6a-5e33-a76a-9d8f3aab99ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f31f1d9-20ae-587f-a12f-646339ce7532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541453} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae6beff-dfb6-5353-a25e-278027e8d1a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43dcffb9-2ca6-59ab-b26c-63732a3440fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-4101" :question/problem "Find $x+y$ if the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(x,y)$ and $(5,-4)$ is $(0,6).$" :question/worked-solution "The given points are ${{(x,y)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1},\\,{y}_{1})}$, ${{(5,-4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2},\\,{y}_{2})}$ and ${{(0,6)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}.$\n\nFirst, the $x$-coordinate of the midpoint's  must be the average of the $x$-coordinates of the endpoints: \n\n$$\n0=\\frac{x+5}{2}\\,⇒\\,x=-5.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the $y$-coordinate of the midpoint must be the average of the $y$-coordinates of the endpoints: \n\n$$\n6=\\frac{y+(-4)}{2}\\,⇒\\,y=16.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(x,y)=(-5,16)$ and $x+y=11.$"}]}
